# oracle: pair_style mgpt (Ta6.8x, 4x4x4 bcc Ta from 2000 K) under fix npt iso: the box changes every step, so the atomic density of the volume terms and the ghost shifts follow it; 4 steps with thermo every step (an energy step natively each time)
# native: b332f28 built with -D PKG_MGPT=on -D PKG_MANYBODY=on -D PKG_MOLECULE=on (serial, 1 process, default CMake Release flags, so the MGPT generic linear algebra; the installed lmp lacks MGPT)
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 3.9e-14, atoms 7.0e-16. The barostat reads the pressure at every step; natively these are all energy steps (thermo 1), so the three- and four-ion volume terms are in it each time.
# oracle-potentials: Ta6.8x.mgpt.parmin Ta6.8x.mgpt.potin
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           electron
atom_style      atomic
variable        atomic_vol equal 121.6
variable        lattice_constant equal (${atomic_vol}*2.0)^(1.0/3.0)
lattice         bcc ${lattice_constant}
region          box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
pair_style      mgpt
pair_coeff      * * Ta6.8x.mgpt.parmin Ta6.8x.mgpt.potin ${atomic_vol}
velocity        all create 2000.0 4242 loop geom
neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
fix             1 all npt temp 2000.0 2000.0 100.0 iso 0.0 0.0 200.0
timestep        2.0
thermo          1
thermo_style    custom step temp pe etotal press vol lx
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             4
